    "summary": "&#039;Clan badge&#039; consisting of two lengths of thick twisted fibre cord knotted together above, and one third above, semicircular pyroincised wooden section, decorated both sides with pale diagonal bands; cord then passes over wood and through central perforation with two loose knots below. Extending down into large tiger nautilus shell (Nautilus macromphalus), with pink-brown natural linear patterning, cord wraps around bundle of red-stained palm leaves, each leaf streamer cut to a blunt end.",
